{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385738-v20-the-green-path","id":1385738,"title":"V20 The Green Path","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-04T21:35:50-07:00","id":1385738,"title":"V20 The Green Path","content":"So I'm about to start a new Chronicle, and one of my players has decided to play her very first Tremere. She thinks The Green Path is cool. However, reading the second level got me to thinking. 5 successes can make a tree grow instantly. Like, I know what that could do: (start at 1:05) <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SDuzExLDAk4\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SDuzExLDAk4</a>. The question is, how do I even rule on that? How much damage are we talking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:44:18-07:00","id":1385740,"title":"","content":"You're not the only one who thought of Redwoods when first reading the power. This, and things like Koldunic Sorcery summoning literal volcanoes, are major levels of power that break low level magic effects.<br /> <br /> But maybe don't treat it like full growth for something like a redwood, maybe it only grows to normal tree height?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:07:12-07:00","id":1385815,"title":"","content":"Of course at that point, I need to define &quot;normal tree height&quot;. There are some difficulties to be sure, if you wanted to use this in combat. (I imagine NERO-style seed packets being whipped at enemies, then the Green Mage does her thing). But out of combat? A lot of damage could be done by a tree. I guess it would be like a grenade going off (though probably bashing damage). I don't mind players being creative, but it's ~slightly~ out of line with what a level 2 Path power should be doing, which is why I was curious what other people thought. Thanks for the reply though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:29:41-07:00","id":1385827,"title":"","content":"I really don't think this power has any &quot;combat&quot; uses in an offensive way.<br /> <br /> It requires the thaumaturge to touch the plant, or in this case seed, so no throwing anything. Also, at five successes, the tree grows to full size (or crumbles to dust) &quot;in a few minutes&quot;, and this basically renders cobat useage to cause damage almost impossible.<br /> <br /> I could see it as a way to potentially damage a structure, like growing a Redwood in a building would do a lot of structural damage, but in a round by round fight, basically useless...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:35:51-07:00","id":1385896,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure you could bypass the need to touch the target by abusing the Principle of Identity in some fashion, but that's a fair point (how hard could it be to research the True Name of a seed?). The &quot;Redwood Grenade&quot; would require some setup to ensure you weren't at ground zero when it goes off, to the point that the time and effort required certainly balance the scales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:46:32-07:00","id":1385901,"title":"","content":"Basic rule of improv: &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yes,_and...\" target=\"_blank\">yes, and</a>&quot;, not &quot;no&quot;. If the player wants to play a plant mage, who will it hurt? Even if it unbalances the game, who will it hurt? Even if you have trouble finding opponents, who will it hurt?<br /> <br /> It can be scary STing with powers you aren't familiar with, but it's really no big deal. Just tell your player you are a little scared of where the power might lead. Sit down with them and do a quick read-through (aloud!) of the power's text. Make sure you're both on the same page. As long as the two of you agree on what it can do, and no other player has an issue with it, you're good to go.<br /> <br /> Oh, and when in doubt about a story element, always err on the side of making it more awesome, not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:04:31-07:00","id":1385904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385738-v20-the-green-path?p=1385896#post1385896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure you could bypass the need to touch the target by abusing the Principle of Identity in some fashion, but that's a fair point (how hard could it be to research the True Name of a seed?). The &amp;quot;Redwood Grenade&amp;quot; would require some setup to ensure you weren't at ground zero when it goes off, to the point that the time and effort required certainly balance the scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hardly call a tree growing to maturity over minutes a &quot;grenade&quot;, it would grow upwards at about 2/3 feet a second and outwards at maybe 4 inches a second, hardly explosive in combat rounds...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:47:14-07:00","id":1385922,"title":"","content":"Ha, somehow I kept missing the &quot;few minutes&quot; in that sentence. Well then, no need to worry about it any longer, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T22:41:22-07:00","id":1386011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385738-v20-the-green-path?p=1385827#post1385827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't think this power has any &quot;combat&quot; uses in an offensive way.<br /> <br /> It requires the thaumaturge to touch the plant, or in this case seed, so no throwing anything. Also, at five successes, the tree grows to full size (or crumbles to dust) &quot;in a few minutes&quot;, and this basically renders cobat useage to cause damage almost impossible.<br /> <br /> I could see it as a way to potentially damage a structure, like growing a Redwood in a building would do a lot of structural damage, but in a round by round fight, basically useless...</div> </div> </div> </div>No there is definite potential, especially as a siege weapon. Grapple a foe and activate it under them, especially if you have someone else do the grappling. Or as a last minute grapple hold say when a Vozhd is about to eat you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T01:21:08-07:00","id":1386024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385738-v20-the-green-path?p=1386011#post1386011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No there is definite potential, especially as a siege weapon. Grapple a foe and activate it under them, especially if you have someone else do the grappling. Or as a last minute grapple hold say when a Vozhd is about to eat you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, if you've got the rounds to hold the grapple, and whoever is holding the grapple is going to get &quot;hit&quot; too. Again, i doubt it's going to really bother a vozhd, the first say, 5/6 rounds the vozhd is going to be too big and strong to be bothered by a sappling and will just get pushed away once it does get big enough.<br /> <br /> I did say it was good for structural damage, but anything more mobile than a wall? Would take crazy circumstances to cause damage...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:33:03-07:00","id":1386454,"title":"","content":"It could be handy for ceremonial stakings, like a quicker version of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bamboo_torture\" target=\"_blank\">bamboo torture</a>. Not so much for a foe who's capable of movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:21:12-07:00","id":1386577,"title":"","content":"Like so many Thaumaturgy paths, the power comes from the personal knowledge of the character &amp; player rather than explicitly from the mechanics. The ability to produce trees by itself isn't a direct combat ability by itself, but if you are setting up an area for combat to happen later, it can become incredibly powerful.<br /> <br /> If you have a group of mortals or ghouls coming after you in the foreseeable future then creating a grove of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J1u460b_hrI\" target=\"_blank\">Manchineel trees</a> in a contained area can be rather deadly, especially if you can then use the path powers to animate the limbs or whole trees. Taking a page from the batman baddy Poison Ivy only takes a little googling to pull off with the Green Path.<br /> <br /> On the other hand you can make the argument that a few toxic trees won't do much to kindred. In direct combat this is correct, unless the enemy took a flaw about garlic, wolfsbane or wild roses. Additionally if your opponent kindred has their hand in the drug trade, what happens to their business model if you use your powers to make huge crops of drug plants spring up ready to harvested practically overnight? Imagine what happens to a Ventrue when they just put in an order for millions of dollars worth of drugs, only to have some one crash the local market by selling for a quarter of the price or just giving it away for free.<br /> <br /> Need to deal with local lupines? Then start growing toxic plants near their kinfolk. Depending on the plant it can contaminate the soil for years or decades with toxins. I mean garlic, onions and chocolate are often toxic to dogs, so they wouldn't automatically know to avoid them any more than the human kinfolk would know to avoid oleander. Yes this approach can take years or decades, but so what, as a vampire you have eternity.<br /> <br /> The Green Path, the Path of Conjuration, and the Path of Technomancy basically are the scariest paths when mixed with real world knowledge. I have seen STs with a decade plus experience under their belt start to really feel the pressure when their players were IRL botanists, hackers, or engineers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}